@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Charts: Analysis)

Correlation matrices, PCA and k-means. Each chart is followed by the source that drew it, and every example carries its own data.

@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Correlation matrix}

Pearson correlation of every numeric column, as a heatmap. The key runs -1 to +1 always, never to the data — so an all-red matrix means everything really is correlated. colormap= changes the scale.

@graph(stat=corr, colormap=coolwarm)
@data
height,weight,age
158,52,24
163,55,31
167,61,28
171,64,45
175,70,39
182,79,52
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(stat=corr, colormap=coolwarm)
@data
